{
 "_about": "Track B blade colours, linear albedo (0..1, the value Unreal's BaseColor takes, not sRGB). root = where the blade leaves the ground, tip = the outer third; parts not listed use the leaf. lawn_bermuda and lawn_rough leaf colours are solved (check_grass.py --solve) so their blades seen from above average to Track A's ground means (_track_a, from Tools/envloop/ground/surfaces.json, Nov 16 provisional, no grey card yet): tips brighter and roots darker than the ground, the same mean, so the fade from blades to texture can't be seen: the tip colours of lawn_bermuda and lawn_rough must equal Track A's lawn and dry-grass albedo within 10 percent so the fade from blades to texture can't be seen. translucency = share of light passing through a leaf (backlit glow), roughness for the specular sheen of a waxy blade. Sources: leaf albedo of turf grasses 0.05 to 0.15 in the visible (USDA/ASD field spectra, green peak 0.12 to 0.18), dormant warm-season turf 0.25 to 0.35; checked against the reference photos by eye until grey-card photos exist. Bunch grasses' summer tips raised Nov 16 to the middle of that green peak (the first renders read too dark against the ground at noon).",
